# UI Components & Styling

- Use [shadcn/ui](https://ui.shadcn.com/) for all new UI components
- Add components via CLI: `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <component>`
- Style with Tailwind utility classes only
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` when merging conditional classes
- Use shadcn theme tokens (`bg-background`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`, etc.) instead of ad-hoc colors
- Custom components only when shadcn has no suitable primitive — build on top of existing shadcn pieces when possible
- Avoid custom CSS files; `app/globals.css` is reserved for shadcn theme variables and Tailwind imports only
